# Raw MSG3 archive (45 real .nat scenes, ~12GB, Nov 2023) -- too large for
# git, and it's raw satellite input, not code/output. Derived JSON/parquet
# outputs in the same folder (hazards_district_nov2023*.json,
# track_e_results.json, grid_dataset.parquet, etc.) are real, small, and kept.
data/msg_oct_nov_2023/nat_in/

# Track H live nowcasting loop (Week 13+): same real reasoning as above --
# the rolling raw .nat window is large binary satellite input, not code/
# output, and regenerates automatically every ~15min the loop runs. The
# derived web_data/msg_hazard grids (small, ~23MB) and the real
# district_alerts_live.json/csv/hazards_district_live.json evidence files
# ARE kept. cycle.lock is ephemeral runtime state, never meaningful to commit.
data/live_nowcast/nat_in/
data/live_nowcast/web_data/_hazard_grid_tmp/
data/live_nowcast/cycle.lock

# Real operational logs and one-off scratch/diagnostic scripts from Track H's
# build (nrt_retry_check.sh, observe_3h.sh) -- contain real local file paths
# (this machine's directory structure) in failure-traceback output, and
# aren't real reusable pipeline code. The real per-cycle pipeline script
# itself (pipelines/scheduler/live_nowcast_cycle.py) IS kept.
logs/
data/live_nowcast/*.sh

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local secrets (never used in this project, kept as a guard rail)
.env
.env.local
*.env
